```

@DamianEdwards Since it doesn't seem like this is coming any time soon, you could accomplish that using the same pattern I provided above. Our goals was to use them in pairs such as 5300/5301 and 6100/6101, etc. For your requirement, you should be able to do the following:

```
httpPort": {
   "type": "generated",
   "generator": "port",
   "parameters": {
      "low": 5000,
      "high": 5300,
      "fallback": 5000
   },
   "replaces": "httpPort"
},
"httpsPort": {
    "type": "generated",
    "generator": "regex",
    "dataType": "string",
    "replaces": "httpsPort",
    "parameters": {
      "source": "httpPort",
      "steps": [
        {
          "regex": "^(\\d)",
          "replacement": "7"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
```

That should generate your httpPort in the range 5000-5300. Then simply replaces the first digit with a 7 for the HTTPS port. So if it generated port 5221, your HTTPS port would be 7221.

